pulse_virus under neuron-monitor at 1 s and 2 s periods -- trn1.2xlarge 2026-09-11.

pulse_virus loads for half of each 2 s cycle (measured cycle ~2.07 s). Once the
monitor period was honoured at 1 s, each sample covered half a cycle. Printed below:
every period's effective_flops for core 0, through the harness (pulse_probe.py
wraps neuron_monitor.whole_period_flops), then the row.

Kernel's own figure for comparison (flops_issued / the 30 s window):
  1 s run: 40.02 TFLOPS  -> monitor Score 38.76, -3.2%
  2 s run: 40.61 TFLOPS  -> monitor Score 40.60, -0.03%
  (the full pass on 1 s periods: kernel 40.68, monitor 39.19, -3.7%)

At 1 s the readings beat against the pulse (14 to 68 TFLOPS) and the Score sits
3-4% under the kernel; a period falling wholly inside an idle half would read 0
and end the busy block. At 2 s every whole period reads 40.67-40.69.
pantheon_neuron.monitor_period_for now asks for whole pulse cycles.

